WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.577 line:0%
[phone ringing]

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.945 line:0%
HOMEY: Hello?

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:16.916 line:0%
NARRATOR: 4:00 PM, Los Angeles,
a drug deal is going down.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.584 line:0%
HOMEY: Alright,
text me the address.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:19.752 line:0%
Alright, check it out.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:22.288 line:0%
I just got an order in
from an A-list actor

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.324 line:0%
who has a premiere tonight.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.029 line:0%
We about to do
a red carpet event.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.398 line:0%
You're going to see how
Hollywood does it, baby.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:39.038 line:0%
Celebrity style, all white,
pimped out, cocaine is the name.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.340 line:0%
NARRATOR: LA gang member Homey
deals coke

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.610 line:0%
to some of the world's
most famous faces.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.847 line:0%
HOMEY: He wants a quarter pound
of the purest cocaine

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.716 line:0%
money can buy.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.585 line:0%
You can instantly even feel it,
it will get your fingers numb,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.522 line:0%
make you gag, and make
your whole face numb.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.828 line:0%
You got to keep this locked
at all times.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.630 line:0%
NARRATOR: Homey's first move
is to visit the stash house...

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.031 line:0%
HOMEY: What's up, G?

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:09.269 line:0%
NARRATOR: ...that he shares with
his fellow gang-banging dealers.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.003 line:0%
HOMEY: Have you got the scale
over there?

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:14.807 line:0%
My client needs a baby brick,

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.978 line:0%
and I know most of these bricks
are going to be right here,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.746 line:0%
look at this [bleep] piece.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:26.519 line:0%
He is going to pay
$4,800 for that.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.120 line:0%
NARRATOR: With so much money
at stake,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.290 line:0%
Homey's taking no chances.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.725 line:0%
[gunshots]

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.462 line:0%
HOMEY: White gold,
it's not always yellow.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.472 line:0%
NARRATOR: In the USA over
four million people

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.375 line:0%
regularly use cocaine.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:53.145 line:0%
This powerful stimulant is
worth more than gold,

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:58.217 line:0%
and every year Americans spend
over $37 billion on the drug.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:01.053 line:0%
[sniffs]

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.789 line:0%
Los Angeles, California,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.159 line:0%
is one of the USA's
largest coke markets.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:06.993 line:0%
HOMEY: Do you know
what is out there?

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.529 line:0%
Millions and millions of dollars

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.031 line:0%
from thousands and thousands
of users.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.867 line:0%
Nice, nice, nice.

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:18.103 line:0%
NARRATOR: Today Homey is dealing
to a world famous actor.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:20.840 line:0%
HOMEY: I got to go to
the red carpet right now, bro.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.841 line:0%
MAN: You got another
movie premiere?

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:25.844 line:0%
HOMEY: Yeah, another
movie premiere.

00:02:25.844 --> 00:02:29.749 line:0%
NARRATOR: His coke is supplied
by his gang on credit.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:33.552 line:0%
HOMEY: I've known my suppliers
as far back as my childhood,

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.521 line:0%
so we're very close-knit,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.123 line:0%
and I don't ever pay
for anything upfront.

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:39.825 line:0%
I have a certain amount
I have to work with

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:44.096 line:0%
and distribute weekly,
and I pay it off as I get it.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:46.865 line:0%
NARRATOR: Homey makes $200
on every ounce.

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:49.902 line:0%
Tonight's deal is worth
big money.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.770 line:0%
HOMEY: I'm dropping off
four ounces,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.374 line:0%
so I will be walking away
with $800 for myself

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.443 line:0%
with nothing out of my pocket
other than gas and my time,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:01.113 line:0%
and that's how
I like to work it.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.415 line:0%
NARRATOR: But to get paid,

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:07.320 line:0%
Homey must deliver the coke
without getting busted.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.821 line:0%
HOMEY: I don't know
what's going on here.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.424 line:0%
We have a lot of
police presence here.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:20.165 line:0%
The last thing we need to do is
[bleep] get pulled over.

00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:22.234 line:0%
NARRATOR: The location of
tonight's deal

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.838 line:0%
is super high risk.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.941 line:0%
HOMEY: Who in the hell would
tell you to do a deal

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.975 line:0%
at a red carpet for God's sakes?

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:33.279 line:0%
Only a [bleep] celebrity.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:37.917 line:0%
And I'm supposed to hand him
his package on the red carpet

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.753 line:0%
in front of everybody
on the planet.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.255 line:0%
And God knows what he is
going to do with it.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:47.092 line:0%
He is buying a little more than
just enough for his head.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:48.795 line:0%
NARRATOR: Cocaine has been
linked to the deaths

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:52.598 line:0%
of a number of Hollywood icons.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.800 line:0%
From River Phoenix

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.336 line:0%
to Whitney Houston,

00:03:57.336 --> 00:04:00.073 line:0%
and most recently,
Philip Seymour Hoffman.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:05.311 line:0%
HOMEY: I don't use coke,
no, I don't.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.313 line:0%
That will only make you
a liability,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.882 line:0%
and there is no room for any
liabilities in this field,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.450 line:0%
and I'm not there
to be their friend,

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.452 line:0%
so I'm not there to be
life of the party.

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:17.123 line:0%
I basically handle what I have
to handle and take off.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.335 line:0%
This is what he chose to do,
not me.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.837 line:0%
This is his meeting spot.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.572 line:0%
I would have preferred to
meet him at his home.

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:37.009 line:0%
My adrenaline is pumping
right now.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.344 line:0%
NARRATOR:
Homey's first challenge

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.979 line:0%
is to get into
tonight's premiere.

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:43.682 line:0%
HOMEY: Where the tickets at,
over there?

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:44.817 line:0%
WOMEN: Hi, are you buying
tickets?

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:45.918 line:0%
HOMEY: No, dear,
I'm on the guest list,

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.453 line:0%
I'm one of the actors
in the film.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:51.290 line:0%
NARRATOR: Using a pre-arranged
false name, Homey is in.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.758 line:0%
HOMEY: I just got my ticket,

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:54.794 line:0%
and now I'm going to give it
to him, handle my business,

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:59.198 line:0%
and then I'm going to expect him
to handle his business.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.267 line:0%
NARRATOR: Now Homey needs
to find the buyer

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:05.571 line:0%
and get rid of the coke quickly.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.940 line:0%
HOMEY: So now I got to run
around and look for this actor.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.376 line:0%
So I don't know if it's
this way or up them ones.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.111 line:0%
Yikes, [bleep]!

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:18.384 line:0%
NARRATOR: In front of a crowd,
the deal needs to be subtle.

00:05:20.052 --> 00:05:21.687 line:0%
WOMAN: My friend was like,
'Say hi to him.'

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.791 line:0%
And I'm just like, okay,
but like, I did, and...

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:27.226 line:0%
NARRATOR: With one
quick movement,

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.228 line:0%
the coke changes hands.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.135 line:0%
HOMEY: It went good,
it went good.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:40.439 line:0%
Tomorrow he deposits what he has
to deposit in my account,

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:43.409 line:0%
and then we're good to go,
4,800 bucks.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:47.813 line:0%
That's why we here in LA,
do it big, y'all.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:51.718 line:0%
NARRATOR: Homey's coke is
produced over 4,500 miles away

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:56.222 line:0%
in the remote, lawless valleys
of the VRAE region of Peru.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:03.562 line:0%
Here cocaine starts life
as coca leaves,

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.932 line:0%
worth just $3 a kilo.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.802 line:0%
This valley is the coca capital
of the world.

00:06:10.802 --> 00:06:14.941 line:0%
Peasant farmers grow over
47,000 tons every year.

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:32.758 line:0%
Today José and his family

00:06:32.758 --> 00:06:35.862 line:0%
plan to reap many months
of hard work.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.841 line:0%
They know the police could
swoop in at any moment.

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.757 line:0%
José risks growing coca

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:08.795 line:0%
because it's 20 times more
profitable than legal crops.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.651 line:0%
But the family will
only make money

00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:35.754 line:0%
if they can avoid
getting busted.

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.825 line:0%
The consequences
would be catastrophic.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:44.764 line:0%
Peru's police destroy illegal
crops wherever they find them.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.102 line:0%
They torch the makeshift labs

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.805 line:0%
used to process
the coca leaves...

00:07:56.808 --> 00:08:00.012 line:0%
...and arrest those suspected
of cocaine production.

00:08:10.188 --> 00:08:15.027 line:0%
But today José is lucky,
the harvest is a success.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:20.098 line:0%
And he's made cocaine's
base material, cocaine paste.

00:08:20.098 --> 00:08:24.136 line:0%
The value has now shot up
from $3 a kilo for leaves

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.939 line:0%
to $900 a kilo for paste.

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:32.511 line:0%
José has 13 kilos, but
the family won't get a penny

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:34.914 line:0%
unless they can get it
to market.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.923 line:0%
The coke's buyer
is 120 miles away

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:47.994 line:0%
across a valley full
of cops and thieves.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:12.184 line:0%
Carlos will make
the coke run with his brother

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:13.920 line:0%
who is just 12.

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:39.277 line:0%
For his part,
Carlos will make $900--

00:09:39.277 --> 00:09:42.315 line:0%
cash he needs to support
his wife and child.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.596 line:0%
The brothers set off.

00:09:57.596 --> 00:10:02.034 line:0%
Ahead are three days of hills,
forests and danger.

00:10:18.217 --> 00:10:20.285 line:0%
From the center
of the VRAE region,

00:10:20.285 --> 00:10:23.322 line:0%
the brothers must travel
120 miles west

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:24.857 line:0%
through treacherous
jungle terrain

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:26.892 line:0%
to reach their cocaine buyer.

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.607 line:0%
The brothers want to
stay off the roads

00:10:42.607 --> 00:10:46.045 line:0%
and out of sight, but there is
a river in their path,

00:10:46.045 --> 00:10:48.881 line:0%
and the only way to cross it
is by bridge.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.687 line:0%
Today the brothers
have walked 40 miles.

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:35.327 line:0%
But as night falls,
they can't afford to relax.

00:11:48.006 --> 00:11:49.875 line:0%
Carlos and Pablo hide the coke

00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:52.378 line:0%
to prevent police busting them
in their sleep.

00:11:59.317 --> 00:12:01.921 line:0%
And to stop thieves
robbing them.

00:12:36.588 --> 00:12:39.424 line:0%
Over the next 40 hours
the brothers cover

00:12:39.424 --> 00:12:42.260 line:0%
70 miles of jungle.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.896 line:0%
The buyer is now close.

00:12:43.896 --> 00:12:45.431 line:0%
[phone ringing]

00:12:54.039 --> 00:12:57.143 line:0%
The race is on to
get to the buyer in time.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.516 line:0%
But suddenly
there's a noise--

00:13:04.516 --> 00:13:06.352 line:0%
a vehicle is approaching.

00:13:10.622 --> 00:13:12.658 line:0%
And it could be a threat.

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.865 line:0%
NARRATOR: Brothers Pablo and
Carlos are dodging police

00:13:19.865 --> 00:13:23.902 line:0%
and thieves on a coke run
that could kill them.

00:13:23.902 --> 00:13:27.439 line:0%
They have heard a noise
and taken cover.

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:29.375 line:0%
But it's only a farmer.

00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:48.561 line:0%
The brothers now have less than
an hour to reach their buyer.

00:14:00.572 --> 00:14:03.676 line:0%
Finally Pablo and Carlos
spot him.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.236 line:0%
The brothers receive the money

00:14:30.236 --> 00:14:33.605 line:0%
that will keep
their family going...

00:14:33.605 --> 00:14:36.275 line:0%
until they have to make
the next coke run.

00:14:49.854 --> 00:14:52.857 line:0%
The cocaine paste has just
entered the supply chain

00:14:52.857 --> 00:14:56.562 line:0%
of a Peruvian drug cartel.

00:14:56.562 --> 00:14:58.430 line:0%
Having made it
out of the jungle,

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.532 line:0%
the paste is refined
into cocaine,

00:15:00.532 --> 00:15:04.870 line:0%
and its value rises from $900
to $1,300 a kilo.

00:15:07.806 --> 00:15:11.143 line:0%
The next stage is to get it
out of the country.

00:15:32.463 --> 00:15:35.867 line:0%
Manuel is in charge of
transporting his cartel's coke

00:15:35.867 --> 00:15:37.836 line:0%
out of the VRAE region.

00:15:52.484 --> 00:15:54.886 line:0%
Today he needs to move
over 800 kilos

00:15:54.886 --> 00:15:57.289 line:0%
to an airfield due north.

00:16:14.973 --> 00:16:17.442 line:0%
Such a huge shipment of coke
is a target

00:16:17.442 --> 00:16:20.112 line:0%
for those on both sides
of the law.

00:16:27.719 --> 00:16:30.723 line:0%
It's even a temptation
for Manuel's drivers.

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:52.844 line:0%
Today's journey passes
without problems.

00:16:52.844 --> 00:16:54.780 line:0%
The coke has made it
to an airfield

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.983 line:0%
in the Pichis-Palcazu area
of central Peru.

00:16:58.983 --> 00:17:02.454 line:0%
But in the region's center,
Constitucion City,

00:17:02.454 --> 00:17:05.190 line:0%
Peruvian police are on the move.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:25.944 line:0%
Colonel Zanabria's unit
is trained to kill.

00:17:37.856 --> 00:17:42.694 line:0%
20 tons of coke are flown out of
this valley every month.

00:17:42.694 --> 00:17:45.531 line:0%
The terrain is well suited
for illegal airfields.

00:18:14.092 --> 00:18:17.963 line:0%
As they approach today's target,
the helicopters hug the terrain

00:18:17.963 --> 00:18:20.766 line:0%
to reduce the risk of locals
spotting them.

00:18:36.848 --> 00:18:39.985 line:0%
The coke traffickers' airfield
is now directly below.

00:18:50.962 --> 00:18:55.134 line:0%
The unit has no idea who or what
is waiting for them.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:19:00.772 line:0%
Colonel Zanabria and his men
could come under fire

00:19:00.772 --> 00:19:02.674 line:0%
at any moment.

00:19:15.887 --> 00:19:17.589 line:0%
NARRATOR: Peru's police
have just landed

00:19:17.589 --> 00:19:20.459 line:0%
on a coke trafficker's
jungle airfield.

00:19:25.397 --> 00:19:28.433 line:0%
A burnt-out plane is the only
sign of the traffickers.

00:19:30.569 --> 00:19:33.105 line:0%
But that could change
at any moment.

00:19:36.975 --> 00:19:40.312 line:0%
Colonel Zanabria sets up
his perimeter guard.

00:19:54.359 --> 00:19:56.328 line:0%
The plan is to blow huge craters

00:19:56.328 --> 00:19:59.164 line:0%
in the airfield's earth
and timber runway.

00:20:08.506 --> 00:20:11.610 line:0%
The unit buries hundreds
of kilos of explosives.

00:20:41.473 --> 00:20:44.209 line:0%
The airfield is now
rigged to blow.

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.792 line:0%
The team is ready
to take to the air.

00:21:08.633 --> 00:21:11.803 line:0%
With the fuse lit,
the countdown is on.

00:21:40.565 --> 00:21:43.268 line:0%
Now the unit needs to
inspect the damage.

00:21:47.071 --> 00:21:49.641 line:0%
The blast has smashed
the runway's timbers.

00:21:55.714 --> 00:21:58.884 line:0%
And the rest of
the airstrip is also unusable.

00:22:07.826 --> 00:22:10.729 line:0%
This airfield is out of action,

00:22:10.729 --> 00:22:14.165 line:0%
but with countless other active
airstrips in this region,

00:22:14.165 --> 00:22:18.502 line:0%
the coke traffickers still have
multiple export options.

00:22:18.502 --> 00:22:22.273 line:0%
And one plane has
just taken off.

00:22:22.273 --> 00:22:25.076 line:0%
Having got past the police
and into the air,

00:22:25.076 --> 00:22:26.844 line:0%
the value of the coke on board

00:22:26.844 --> 00:22:31.149 line:0%
has soared from $1,300
to $10,000 a kilo.

00:22:34.185 --> 00:22:39.391 line:0%
From Peru it's headed north
to Central America.

00:22:39.391 --> 00:22:42.727 line:0%
But the traffickers can't count
on it getting there,

00:22:42.727 --> 00:22:44.796 line:0%
because US Customs and
Border Protection

00:22:44.796 --> 00:22:46.765 line:0%
have received a tip-off.

00:22:48.934 --> 00:22:52.537 line:0%
And a high-tech P3 surveillance
plane has been scrambled

00:22:52.537 --> 00:22:54.206 line:0%
to intercept.

00:23:21.599 --> 00:23:25.103 line:0%
The P3 has a range
of 5,000 miles,

00:23:25.103 --> 00:23:29.441 line:0%
allowing it to find and follow
drug planes over vast areas.

00:23:31.676 --> 00:23:35.547 line:0%
Its four-bladed turbo props are
much quieter than jet engines,

00:23:35.547 --> 00:23:39.451 line:0%
and operating at night, the
air frame is nearly invisible.

00:23:43.087 --> 00:23:44.956 line:0%
Tonight the crew's
first challenge

00:23:44.956 --> 00:23:47.626 line:0%
is to find
the coke traffickers' plane.

00:23:47.626 --> 00:23:50.862 line:0%
All they know is that
it's over Venezuela.

00:23:53.265 --> 00:23:55.733 line:0%
But they have state-of-the-art
technology,

00:23:55.733 --> 00:24:00.138 line:0%
three advanced radar systems,
and a camera so powerful

00:24:00.138 --> 00:24:03.942 line:0%
it could read the name on
a vessel stern from the air.

00:24:08.313 --> 00:24:11.416 line:0%
Suddenly the traffickers' plane
is in their sights.

00:24:19.391 --> 00:24:22.226 line:0%
The pilot turns
into close pursuit.

00:24:22.226 --> 00:24:25.163 line:0%
The P3 needs to be near enough
to track the plane.

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:31.036 line:0%
But not so close
tha0t they get spotted.

00:24:37.709 --> 00:24:40.978 line:0%
The crew must follow the plane
until it lands.

00:24:40.978 --> 00:24:44.382 line:0%
Its destination could be
thousands of miles away.

00:24:56.661 --> 00:24:58.430 line:0%
But it's not going to be easy.

00:24:58.430 --> 00:25:01.333 line:0%
Four hours in,
and there's a problem.

00:25:01.333 --> 00:25:02.834 line:0%
PILOT: Ahh.

00:25:06.938 --> 00:25:08.473 line:0%
[thunder]

00:25:22.921 --> 00:25:25.390 line:0%
NARRATOR: Flying in
total darkness,

00:25:25.390 --> 00:25:28.426 line:0%
the P3 tracks the plane
through the storm.

00:25:40.038 --> 00:25:42.139 line:0%
After an hour of
extreme turbulence,

00:25:42.139 --> 00:25:43.708 line:0%
the weather subsides.

00:25:48.646 --> 00:25:50.448 line:0%
But 25 minutes later,

00:25:50.448 --> 00:25:52.784 line:0%
there is another
even bigger problem.

00:26:05.763 --> 00:26:09.100 line:0%
They don't have permission
to fly over Belize's airspace.

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:11.036 line:0%
The P3 can't follow.

00:26:28.953 --> 00:26:30.622 line:0%
NARRATOR: US Customs has
lost contact

00:26:30.622 --> 00:26:33.758 line:0%
with the coke plane
they're tracking.

00:26:33.758 --> 00:26:35.293 line:0%
ORIE: You got to get him here,
guys.

00:26:35.293 --> 00:26:36.961 line:0%
OPERATOR:
Yeah, I'm looking for him.

00:26:36.961 --> 00:26:39.663 line:0%
NARRATOR: Based on the plane's
last known course,

00:26:39.663 --> 00:26:43.467 line:0%
the crew are gambling that
it's headed for Guatemala.

00:26:43.467 --> 00:26:46.136 line:0%
PILOT: We should be able to get
him on the radar if he's there.

00:26:46.136 --> 00:26:48.206 line:0%
I don't got anything.

00:26:51.375 --> 00:26:53.844 line:0%
OPERATOR: Oh, look at this.
Absolutely.

00:26:53.844 --> 00:26:55.813 line:0%
PILOT: We got lucky.

00:26:55.813 --> 00:26:57.082 line:0%
OPERATOR: That's not luck.

00:26:57.082 --> 00:26:59.317 line:0%
Nice work, dude.

00:26:59.317 --> 00:27:02.820 line:0%
He's passing into Guatemala,
and I got him.

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:04.689 line:0%
PILOT: See if we can lock
that bad boy up.

00:27:04.689 --> 00:27:06.524 line:0%
Stay, stay with him
while we can now.

00:27:06.524 --> 00:27:08.126 line:0%
PILOT: Okay.

00:27:08.126 --> 00:27:10.161 line:0%
NARRATOR: The coke bust
is back on,

00:27:10.161 --> 00:27:13.064 line:0%
and local police helicopters
are scrambled.

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:14.565 line:0%
PILOT: I am going to recommend
the helicopters turn west

00:27:14.565 --> 00:27:17.668 line:0%
to follow this guy.

00:27:17.668 --> 00:27:20.805 line:0%
NARRATOR: But then after another
hour of pursuit,

00:27:20.805 --> 00:27:25.142 line:0%
the plane takes an evasive turn
to lose any potential tails.

00:27:25.142 --> 00:27:26.043 line:0%
PILOT: What is he doing?

00:27:26.043 --> 00:27:27.545 line:0%
PILOT: I don't know.

00:27:27.545 --> 00:27:29.780 line:0%
Looks like he's going to be on
the border of Mexico, Guatemala.

00:27:29.780 --> 00:27:33.017 line:0%
NARRATOR: The P3 has the range
to follow the new course.

00:27:33.017 --> 00:27:36.020 line:0%
PILOT: Helicopters
cannot refuel.

00:27:36.020 --> 00:27:36.954 line:0%
NARRATOR: But local
law enforcement

00:27:36.954 --> 00:27:39.323 line:0%
has to return to base.

00:27:39.323 --> 00:27:42.360 line:0%
OPERATOR: [bleep], not after
all this.

00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:44.495 line:0%
PILOT: He's dropping lower.
PILOT: He's across the beach.

00:27:44.495 --> 00:27:47.465 line:0%
NARRATOR: As the plane descends
in southwest Guatemala,

00:27:47.465 --> 00:27:50.334 line:0%
all the crew can do is watch.

00:27:50.334 --> 00:27:52.403 line:0%
PILOT: He's landed.
He's on the ground.

00:27:52.403 --> 00:27:53.404 line:0%
PILOT: He's on the ground.

00:27:53.404 --> 00:27:55.306 line:0%
PILOT: That looked like
a crash landing.

00:27:55.306 --> 00:27:56.540 line:0%
PILOT: Oh, what was that?

00:27:56.540 --> 00:27:58.042 line:0%
PILOT: Trucks pulling up.

00:27:58.042 --> 00:28:00.778 line:0%
NARRATOR: Within seconds, a
fleet of trucks offload the coke

00:28:00.778 --> 00:28:02.146 line:0%
and drive off...

00:28:02.146 --> 00:28:04.849 line:0%
PILOT: They're moving off,
they're moving.

00:28:04.849 --> 00:28:08.986 line:0%
NARRATOR: ...where even
the P3 can't track them.

00:28:08.986 --> 00:28:11.723 line:0%
OPERATOR: I lost them
behind tree.

00:28:14.392 --> 00:28:16.394 line:0%
Could they have stopped
at that house?

00:28:16.394 --> 00:28:19.631 line:0%
Hard to tell.

00:28:19.631 --> 00:28:21.232 line:0%
NARRATOR: Despite seven
and a half hours

00:28:21.232 --> 00:28:25.369 line:0%
of successful tracking,
the mission has failed.

00:28:25.369 --> 00:28:27.771 line:0%
PILOT: Let's RTB,
just get out of here.

00:28:27.771 --> 00:28:29.074 line:0%
ORIE: Part of the problem
with us

00:28:29.074 --> 00:28:30.741 line:0%
is we can stay out
for a good while,

00:28:30.741 --> 00:28:33.878 line:0%
we can stay longer than
just about anybody else.

00:28:33.878 --> 00:28:38.182 line:0%
You run out of good guys, and
that's kind of the case tonight.

00:28:38.182 --> 00:28:40.351 line:0%
That's it.

00:28:40.351 --> 00:28:41.352 line:0%
NARRATOR: As the crew return

00:28:41.352 --> 00:28:43.455 line:0%
to their secret
Central American base...

00:28:43.455 --> 00:28:45.690 line:0%
PILOT: Magenta line is
the road home.

00:28:45.690 --> 00:28:47.424 line:0%
PILOT: Gotcha.

00:28:47.424 --> 00:28:50.294 line:0%
NARRATOR: Everyone knows
where the coke is headed.

00:28:50.294 --> 00:28:53.531 line:0%
PILOT: He's going to go to
Mexico, man, I bet you.

00:28:53.531 --> 00:28:56.167 line:0%
ORIE: The trucks were moving
towards Mexico.

00:28:56.167 --> 00:28:58.436 line:0%
That's definitely
where it's going.

00:29:00.471 --> 00:29:02.840 line:0%
NARRATOR: From Guatemala,
the coke is headed to Mexico

00:29:02.840 --> 00:29:05.210 line:0%
into the hands of the cartels.

00:29:08.446 --> 00:29:12.716 line:0%
Having got past Peruvian police
and US surveillance planes,

00:29:12.716 --> 00:29:17.155 line:0%
the coke's value has shot up
from $10,000 to $14,000 a kilo.

00:29:20.525 --> 00:29:23.627 line:0%
But it's worth twice that
in the USA.

00:29:23.627 --> 00:29:25.930 line:0%
To get it there, drug runners
have a tunnel running

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:30.502 line:0%
from Tijuana all the way under
the border to San Diego.

00:29:33.304 --> 00:29:37.608 line:0%
LENOIR: We are actually heading
over to a discovered tunnel.

00:29:37.608 --> 00:29:39.077 line:0%
We are going to get in there,

00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:41.379 line:0%
and we are actually working into

00:29:41.379 --> 00:29:43.548 line:0%
putting the tunnel
out of action.

00:29:49.053 --> 00:29:51.455 line:0%
NARRATOR: Agent Lenoir's team
has uncovered the entrance

00:29:51.455 --> 00:29:55.627 line:0%
to a 1,600-foot tunnel hidden
inside a warehouse.

00:29:57.995 --> 00:30:00.932 line:0%
It's his job to discover
what's inside.

00:30:05.002 --> 00:30:07.938 line:0%
LENOIR: The noise you hear are
air handlers in there

00:30:07.938 --> 00:30:10.241 line:0%
that are to establish our own
air ventilation in there

00:30:10.241 --> 00:30:11.642 line:0%
to get enough oxygen in there

00:30:11.642 --> 00:30:16.247 line:0%
so we can actually map this
thing and see where it goes.

00:30:16.247 --> 00:30:22.120 line:0%
NARRATOR: He needs to map the
tunnel so it can be demolished.

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:25.056 line:0%
But this tunnel could be deadly.

00:30:27.492 --> 00:30:31.362 line:0%
LENOIR: And we're going in.

00:30:31.362 --> 00:30:36.700 line:0%
The worst part in there is
we are at risk of a collapse.

00:30:36.700 --> 00:30:43.140 line:0%
Obviously, running out of air is
a critical concern as well.

00:30:43.140 --> 00:30:44.975 line:0%
NARRATOR: The Sinaloa Cartel
built this tunnel

00:30:44.975 --> 00:30:47.811 line:0%
with little regard
for human life.

00:30:47.811 --> 00:30:50.381 line:0%
LENOIR: The actual laborers
or workers,

00:30:50.381 --> 00:30:52.850 line:0%
they are worried about
the same thing we are.

00:30:52.850 --> 00:30:54.318 line:0%
It is probably a safe assumption

00:30:54.318 --> 00:30:56.387 line:0%
that several people have
actually perished

00:30:56.387 --> 00:30:59.857 line:0%
in the construction of
these particular tunnels.

00:30:59.857 --> 00:31:02.293 line:0%
NARRATOR: To stay alive,
Agent Lenoir must rely on

00:31:02.293 --> 00:31:05.529 line:0%
his wits and his
emergency gas meter.

00:31:05.529 --> 00:31:09.066 line:0%
LENOIR: We are always equipped
with a four gas meter.

00:31:09.066 --> 00:31:11.135 line:0%
It tells us what
our oxygen levels are.

00:31:11.135 --> 00:31:14.906 line:0%
It also indicates any other
dangerous atmospheric conditions

00:31:14.906 --> 00:31:17.341 line:0%
we may encounter.

00:31:17.341 --> 00:31:19.944 line:0%
NARRATOR: The further he gets
from the surface...

00:31:19.944 --> 00:31:21.512 line:0%
LENOIR: I can feel it getting
a little bit cooler.

00:31:21.512 --> 00:31:23.414 line:0%
Watch your step right here.

00:31:23.414 --> 00:31:26.083 line:0%
NARRATOR: The less air he has...

00:31:26.083 --> 00:31:29.053 line:0%
LENOIR: We're up to 20% oxygen
right now.

00:31:29.053 --> 00:31:30.888 line:0%
NARRATOR: ...and the further
he is from help

00:31:30.888 --> 00:31:32.990 line:0%
if the tunnel collapses.

00:31:32.990 --> 00:31:35.226 line:0%
LENOIR: We know that the tunnel
is going to collapse,

00:31:35.226 --> 00:31:37.662 line:0%
it's just a question of when.

00:31:44.535 --> 00:31:49.606 line:0%
NARRATOR: 35 feet down, he
finally reaches a flat stretch.

00:31:49.606 --> 00:31:52.043 line:0%
LENOIR: We are in the guts of
the tunnel right now,

00:31:52.043 --> 00:31:55.412 line:0%
we got a rail system right here,

00:31:55.412 --> 00:31:58.315 line:0%
and there is the cart that
they were actually using

00:31:58.315 --> 00:32:02.419 line:0%
to push tons of narcotics
through.

00:32:02.419 --> 00:32:04.388 line:0%
NARRATOR:
For the Sinaloa Cartel,

00:32:04.388 --> 00:32:06.023 line:0%
this tunnel was
a huge investment

00:32:06.023 --> 00:32:10.661 line:0%
in time, money and resources.

00:32:10.661 --> 00:32:13.731 line:0%
LENOIR: Alright, we are just now
passing the 100-meter mark.

00:32:13.731 --> 00:32:15.199 line:0%
NARRATOR: As he takes
the measurements needed

00:32:15.199 --> 00:32:17.068 line:0%
to take down their operation...

00:32:17.068 --> 00:32:19.737 line:0%
LENOIR: That will give us
a fairly accurate idea

00:32:19.737 --> 00:32:23.307 line:0%
on where the tunnel is
in relation to the surface.

00:32:23.307 --> 00:32:26.144 line:0%
NARRATOR: Agent Lenoir knows
he's vulnerable.

00:32:26.144 --> 00:32:28.913 line:0%
LENOIR: There is nobody actually
guarding the south side,

00:32:28.913 --> 00:32:32.050 line:0%
because that end is
actually vacant.

00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:35.186 line:0%
NARRATOR: At any moment,
he could have company.

00:32:42.526 --> 00:32:45.095 line:0%
NARRATOR: Agent Lenoir is
in a cartel tunnel

00:32:45.095 --> 00:32:48.599 line:0%
getting the coordinates
he needs to take it out.

00:32:52.036 --> 00:32:55.372 line:0%
The job could kill him
if he suffocates...

00:32:55.372 --> 00:32:57.742 line:0%
LENOIR: We used up quite
a bit of oxygen already.

00:32:57.742 --> 00:33:01.578 line:0%
NARRATOR: ...or gets crushed
by a collapse.

00:33:01.578 --> 00:33:04.715 line:0%
LENOIR: This might actually
might be a fault right here.

00:33:04.715 --> 00:33:07.618 line:0%
You can see it differs from
the more cemented sandstone

00:33:07.618 --> 00:33:10.555 line:0%
we have on either side of it.

00:33:13.457 --> 00:33:15.793 line:0%
NARRATOR: 1,000 feet in,
he finally reaches

00:33:15.793 --> 00:33:21.499 line:0%
the last stretch of the tunnel
under US soil.

00:33:21.499 --> 00:33:25.003 line:0%
LENOIR: Alright, I am going to
take one last compass reading.

00:33:27.171 --> 00:33:29.040 line:0%
We got everything we need
inside this tunnel,

00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:33.478 line:0%
so we are going to actually
travel, head back north.

00:33:35.279 --> 00:33:38.315 line:0%
NARRATOR: Agent Lenoir is
heading back to safety.

00:33:38.315 --> 00:33:39.683 line:0%
But with billions of dollars
to be made

00:33:39.683 --> 00:33:41.886 line:0%
moving coke across the border,

00:33:41.886 --> 00:33:46.624 line:0%
he knows this tunnel
won't be his last.

00:33:46.624 --> 00:33:50.228 line:0%
LENOIR: Officially there have
been 169 tunnels

00:33:50.228 --> 00:33:51.995 line:0%
throughout both our borders.

00:33:51.995 --> 00:33:54.898 line:0%
When you have suitable areas
in which to tunnel

00:33:54.898 --> 00:33:59.870 line:0%
and you have the willingness
on somebody to do that work,

00:33:59.870 --> 00:34:03.875 line:0%
the threat of tunneling is
always going to be there.

00:34:07.044 --> 00:34:08.780 line:0%
Voilà.

00:34:11.349 --> 00:34:13.183 line:0%
NARRATOR: Using Agent Lenoir's
coordinates,

00:34:13.183 --> 00:34:16.120 line:0%
holes are drilled down
into the tunnel.

00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:19.590 line:0%
Next concrete will be poured
into the shaft.

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:20.924 line:0%
LENOIR: Well, that's it,
nobody goes back in,

00:34:20.924 --> 00:34:22.426 line:0%
we're done pretty much
with this tunnel,

00:34:22.426 --> 00:34:26.364 line:0%
we're going to start filling her
up and move on to the next one.

00:34:29.800 --> 00:34:31.769 line:0%
NARRATOR: This tunnel is
out of action,

00:34:31.769 --> 00:34:35.339 line:0%
but some of the Peruvian coke
got through.

00:34:38.142 --> 00:34:39.644 line:0%
From the border it's trafficked

00:34:39.644 --> 00:34:44.282 line:0%
along the notorious I-5
smuggling route to Los Angeles.

00:34:46.883 --> 00:34:49.220 line:0%
Having got past
cops and customs,

00:34:49.220 --> 00:34:54.659 line:0%
the coke has shot up in value
from $14,000 to $28,000 a kilo.

00:35:00.698 --> 00:35:04.135 line:0%
POUND DOG: This is what you call
cocaine money.

00:35:04.135 --> 00:35:09.407 line:0%
I would kill a [bleep]
for this life here.

00:35:15.112 --> 00:35:17.982 line:0%
NARRATOR: Pound Dog is one of
LA's biggest dealers,

00:35:17.982 --> 00:35:21.052 line:0%
selling cartel coke
on a wholesale level.

00:35:25.956 --> 00:35:28.159 line:0%
POUND DOG: Working for
the cartel, I can go over there

00:35:28.159 --> 00:35:30.093 line:0%
and be like, man, I'm going to
just take one kilo

00:35:30.093 --> 00:35:34.799 line:0%
on credit today,
or you know, 4 or 5 or 100.

00:35:34.799 --> 00:35:36.200 line:0%
Damn.

00:35:38.035 --> 00:35:40.337 line:0%
NARRATOR: Tonight he is
preparing five kilos

00:35:40.337 --> 00:35:43.474 line:0%
for a $140,000 deal.

00:35:52.950 --> 00:35:57.020 line:0%
NARRATOR: If it comes off,
he makes 30 grand.

00:35:57.020 --> 00:35:58.856 line:0%
POUND DOG: Since I'm plugged in
with the Mexicans,

00:35:58.856 --> 00:36:01.058 line:0%
it's kind of like
hitting the lottery.

00:36:01.058 --> 00:36:05.162 line:0%
I made in a week
half a million, easy.

00:36:05.162 --> 00:36:08.632 line:0%
NARRATOR: He is certain
the buyer will like the product.

00:36:08.632 --> 00:36:10.534 line:0%
POUND DOG: Peruvian flake,

00:36:10.534 --> 00:36:12.536 line:0%
that's that good [bleep]
right there.

00:36:12.536 --> 00:36:13.570 line:0%
[laughs]

00:36:13.570 --> 00:36:15.639 line:0%
That's what they all want.

00:36:15.639 --> 00:36:18.175 line:0%
NARRATOR: But he's not so sure
he'll like the buyer,

00:36:18.175 --> 00:36:20.311 line:0%
because he's never met him.

00:36:27.751 --> 00:36:30.454 line:0%
NARRATOR: There's a risk
this deal could turn sour,

00:36:30.454 --> 00:36:32.790 line:0%
and Pound Dog can't afford
to make any mistakes

00:36:32.790 --> 00:36:35.692 line:0%
with the cartel's coke.

00:36:35.692 --> 00:36:38.162 line:0%
POUND DOG: You come back to
the Mexicans without that money,

00:36:38.162 --> 00:36:39.563 line:0%
it gets ugly, you know.

00:36:39.563 --> 00:36:42.065 line:0%
If they can't get you,
they will get your momma,

00:36:42.065 --> 00:36:45.802 line:0%
get your kids snatched up,
get you [bleep] beat up.

00:36:45.802 --> 00:36:47.304 line:0%
Believe it, they will come

00:36:47.304 --> 00:36:49.573 line:0%
[bleep] your [bleep]
all the way up.

00:36:49.573 --> 00:36:51.876 line:0%
It's just a [bleep] nightmare.

00:36:54.678 --> 00:36:57.081 line:0%
NARRATOR: For his and
the coke's safety,

00:36:57.081 --> 00:36:59.550 line:0%
Pound Dog counts on
his reputation.

00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:01.152 line:0%
POUND DOG: I can honestly say
I have done a lot of [bleep]

00:37:01.152 --> 00:37:02.886 line:0%
to get where I am.

00:37:02.886 --> 00:37:04.287 line:0%
But if I want somebody killed,

00:37:04.287 --> 00:37:07.391 line:0%
you best believe your ass
is going to go, you know.

00:37:07.391 --> 00:37:08.793 line:0%
With the violence comes fear,

00:37:08.793 --> 00:37:11.361 line:0%
and with the fear
comes the respect.

00:37:11.361 --> 00:37:12.563 line:0%
[laughs]

00:37:12.563 --> 00:37:14.498 line:0%
I never [bleep].

00:37:21.838 --> 00:37:23.140 line:0%
NARRATOR: Pound Dog is about
to find out

00:37:23.140 --> 00:37:26.344 line:0%
if he'll need to get
violent tonight.

00:37:45.929 --> 00:37:48.532 line:0%
NARRATOR: Reassured the guy
isn't out to rob him,

00:37:48.532 --> 00:37:50.735 line:0%
Pound Dog gets out a sample.

00:38:02.746 --> 00:38:04.715 line:0%
NARRATOR: The buyer agrees
to the deal.

00:38:04.715 --> 00:38:09.085 line:0%
Five kilos is on the move,

00:38:09.085 --> 00:38:13.024 line:0%
heading to West Hollywood,
a club and party mecca.

00:38:16.226 --> 00:38:21.365 line:0%
Here, sold off in grams, the
coke jumps in value from $28,000

00:38:21.365 --> 00:38:25.803 line:0%
to its final price
of $80,000 a kilo.

00:38:28.606 --> 00:38:33.177 line:0%
And one user has just got
her Peruvian product.

00:38:33.177 --> 00:38:35.279 line:0%
COCO: Well, tonight
it's Friday night,

00:38:35.279 --> 00:38:38.381 line:0%
in Los Angeles, California,
in Hollywood,

